# S-044: resampler hook (fake resampler: output = input*0.5, out frames = in_frames*dst_rate/src_rate unless
# overridden, ts_offset configurable). The callback of a converting input receives the resampler's output, its frame
# count, and timestamp - offset. A failing resample skips that input's callback for the tick only.
aopen main 48000 FLOAT_PLANAR STEREO
afeed 0 0 0 2 0.5 set
afeed 0 1 0 1 -0.75 set
anewts delta 0
aprobe 0 1 2
# creation arguments are (dst = input's wish, src = output format)
aconnect a 1 0 24000 - - 0
aconnect b 2 0 - - - 0
resamp offset 1000
atick
resamp offset 0
resamp resample fail
atick
resamp resample ok
resamp frames 7
atick
# creation failure -> connect returns false, nothing registered
resamp create fail
aconnect a 3 0 44100 FLOAT_PLANAR STEREO 0
adump
resamp create ok
# disconnecting a converting input destroys its resampler; close destroys the remaining ones
adisconnect a 1 0
aconnect a 4 1 96000 - - 0
aclose
